# Paths `just check` reads. `scripts/gate-fresh` hashes exactly this set to
# decide whether the last recorded pass (via `scripts/gated-check`) is still
# valid for the current worktree — this is the freshness assertion the
# `[[on.flip]]` predicate in .mindtape/config.toml points at, standing in for
# `mmz --is-fresh -- just check` (mmz is not available in this environment;
# see CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. A directory is walked
# recursively. A line starting with `!` excludes a path (matched as an exact
# path, a directory prefix, or a glob pattern containing `*` — `*` matches
# within one path segment, same as a shell glob, so `examples/*/build`
# matches `examples/kilbil/build` but not `examples/kilbil/x/build`) from an
# include already listed above it. A line starting with `?` includes a path
# (directory, walked recursively) by NAME ONLY: each file under it
# contributes its path to the hash but never its content, so adding,
# removing or renaming a file there changes the result and editing one in
# place does not. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# CRITICAL: truth/tasks is excluded and MUST STAY excluded. `mt flip` writes
# the task file it is gating (the status field, the note), so if task
# artifacts were part of this hash, recording a pass and then flipping a
# single task would change the hash out from under itself and no second
# flip could ever be fresh again. Every other input here is something only a
# real change to the gate's own behaviour touches.
#
# What this hash answers, and what it deliberately does not: this file
# drives FRESHNESS — "has anything the gate reads changed since the last
# recorded pass" — never VALIDITY — "does the tree the gate reads still
# parse". Those are different questions, and truth/tasks is exactly where
# they come apart: a malformed task artifact does not change this hash (see
# above), so freshness alone would let it record as, or read as, a fresh
# pass while `speconaut check truth/` — which `just check` runs via
# `check-specs` — fails on it. `scripts/gate-fresh is-valid` is the second,
# stateless predicate that answers the validity question instead, by
# re-running `speconaut check truth/` (~1s) directly rather than teaching
# this hash to see truth/tasks. Both predicates gate `mt flip ... done`; see
# the `[[on.flip]]` block in .mindtape/config.toml. Do not try to collapse
# them into one hash — that is the mistake this comment exists to head off.

bin
devbox.d
scripts
src
runtime
tests
examples
truth
!truth/tasks

# examples/*/build is each example's own PHPStan tmpDir —
# examples/<name>/phpstan.neon sets `tmpDir: ./build/cache/phpstan`, and
# `just check`'s lint-phpstan-generated step runs `just check` inside every
# examples/*/ directory, so every `just check` writes there. Each
# examples/<name>/.gitignore already ignores it alongside vendor/ and
# composer.lock, same as the root build/ tree (never in this file's include
# list at all) ignores the root tool caches.
#
# It is not byte-stable run over run — reproduced 2026-08-04 by running
# `just check` twice in a row in examples/kilbil with nothing else touched,
# then again via two full `scripts/gated-check` / `just check` passes with
# zero tracked changes in between (`git status --porcelain` and `git diff
# --stat` both empty): the recorded hash still went stale.
# `build/cache/phpstan/cache/nette.configurator/container.journal` changes
# content every run (`Container_c74faa8208:<unix-timestamp>`, minted fresh
# by Nette's DI container journal), and
# `build/cache/phpstan/cache/PHPStan/cache-cleared` (content `v2-new`)
# appeared on the second run where it was absent on the first — so even the
# SET of file names under build/ is unstable, and tracking it by name only
# (the `?` mechanism below) would still flip freshness on an untouched tree.
# Fully excluded, not name-only, for that reason.
#
# Irrelevant to whether the gate ran: build/ is PHPStan's own scratch cache,
# never something `just check` reads as an input that decides whether it
# would still pass, and no reviewer would call cache content "the work" —
# what IS the work stays hashed by the `examples` include above:
# examples/*/generated, examples/*/src, and each example's own
# phpstan.neon and Justfile.
#
# A glob, not four literal paths, because a hand-enumerated list is exactly
# the kind of set that goes stale unnoticed — see `./*.md` further down for
# the same lesson learned once already on this file. `scripts/gate-fresh`'s
# exclude matching understands `*` in a pattern for this reason.
!examples/*/build

# `truth/notes` and `truth/reviews` are Markdown, never `#include`-d into
# `truth/main.typ` — main.typ's own "Supplementary artefacts" section
# `#link`s each one instead, and `#link` is a hyperlink annotation, not a
# compile-time read. `speconaut check truth/` (run by `check-specs`) proves
# both halves of that, verified by probing on 2026-08-03: appending a line to
# an already-linked note's or review's content in place leaves `check truth/`
# green (content is never parsed); adding a file under either directory with
# no matching `#link` fails it with "file not included in entry point", and
# deleting a file main.typ still links to fails it with "broken link target"
# (both proven the same day against a scratch copy of the tree, not assumed).
# So the set of file NAMES present is read for reachability even though no
# file's content is — hashing content here would invalidate a recorded pass
# on every session note written (the bug this file exists to fix); hashing
# nothing here would let a real orphan or broken-link failure record as
# fresh (the same bug from the other side). `?` tracks exactly what is read:
# presence, not content.
?truth/notes
?truth/reviews

composer.json
composer.lock
devbox.json
devbox.lock
Justfile
phpstan.neon.dist
phpstan-generated.neon
rector.php
.php-cs-fixer.dist.php
.jscpd.json
.jscpd.generated.json
.linecop.yaml
phpunit.xml.dist
.speconaut/config.toml

# `.linecop.yaml` caps Markdown at 300 lines and PHP at 250, repo-wide,
# excluding only vendor, build, .devbox, .git, tests/generated,
# tests/fixtures and examples (see its own comments) — and, verified by
# probing on 2026-08-03, every directory whose name starts with `.`: a
# 400-line scratch file under `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/` was not flagged,
# while the identical file at the repo root was. That is why `.github`'s
# Markdown templates need no entry here despite not being in
# `exclude_dirs`.
#
# `./<pattern>` matches root-level files by name and recurses into nothing,
# which is the one thing a directory include cannot express at the repo root.
# It replaces an enumeration of seven Markdown files written on 2026-08-03
# that was already wrong by that afternoon: splitting `AGENT.md` created
# `AGENT_HAZARDS.md`, linecop capped it like every other root document, and
# the list did not know. A set that grows cannot be maintained by hand beside
# the thing that grows it.
./*.md

# `just check` runs `speconaut lock --check`, which reads this file, so a lock
# that changes without the specs changing alters what the gate would say. Only
# a deliberate `speconaut lock` writes it — `mt flip` never does — so hashing
# it costs nothing and closes the case where a re-locked or hand-edited lock
# leaves a recorded pass claiming to cover a tree the gate would now reject.
.speconaut/state.lock
